<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "014, Core dumps restritos, Média"
  info        : "Restringe a geração de core dumps para evitar vazamento de informações sensíveis."
  solution    : "Persistir o parâmetro em /etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf e aplicar com sysctl --system após validar a rede e a carga de trabalho."
  reference   : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  see_also    : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  cmd         : "( [ \"$(sysctl -n fs.suid_dumpable 2>/dev/null)\" = \"0\" ] && grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*fs\\.suid_dumpable[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*0([[:space:]]|$)' /etc/sysctl.d/99-hitss-hardening.conf 2>/dev/null && awk -F= -v key='fs.suid_dumpable' -v expected='0' '{ name=$1; gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",name); if (name==key) { value=$2; sub(/[[:space:]]*[#;].*$/,\"\",value); gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",value) } } END { exit value != expected }' /etc/sysctl.conf 2>/dev/null ) && echo PASS || echo FAIL"
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*PASS\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "015, SUID dump off, Média"
  info        : "Evita que processos SUID gerem dumps com conteúdo sensível gravado em disco."
  solution    : "Persistir o parâmetro em /etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf e aplicar com sysctl --system após validar a rede e a carga de trabalho."
  reference   : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  see_also    : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  cmd         : "( [ \"$(sysctl -n fs.suid_dumpable 2>/dev/null)\" = \"0\" ] && grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*fs\\.suid_dumpable[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*0([[:space:]]|$)' /etc/sysctl.d/99-hitss-hardening.conf 2>/dev/null && awk -F= -v key='fs.suid_dumpable' -v expected='0' '{ name=$1; gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",name); if (name==key) { value=$2; sub(/[[:space:]]*[#;].*$/,\"\",value); gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",value) } } END { exit value != expected }' /etc/sysctl.conf 2>/dev/null ) && echo PASS || echo FAIL"
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*PASS\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "016, NX/XD ativo, Alta"
  info        : "Garante que a execução de código em áreas de memória não é permitida."
  solution    : "Ajustar o controle 'NX/XD ativo' conforme a política aprovada para Debian-like 11+."
  reference   : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  see_also    : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  cmd         : "( case \"$(uname -m)\" in x86_64|i?86) grep -qw nx /proc/cpuinfo ;; *) grep -Eq '^CONFIG_STRICT_KERNEL_RWX=y' /boot/config-$(uname -r) 2>/dev/null ;; esac ) && echo PASS || echo NA && echo PASS || echo NA && echo PASS || echo NA"
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*(PASS|NA)\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "017, ASLR habilitado, Alta"
  info        : "Randomização de espaço de memória dificulta exploits baseados em endereço fixo."
  solution    : "Persistir o parâmetro em /etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf e aplicar com sysctl --system após validar a rede e a carga de trabalho."
  reference   : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  see_also    : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  cmd         : "( [ \"$(sysctl -n kernel.randomize_va_space 2>/dev/null)\" = \"2\" ] && grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*kernel\\.randomize_va_space[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*2([[:space:]]|$)' /etc/sysctl.d/99-hitss-hardening.conf 2>/dev/null && awk -F= -v key='kernel.randomize_va_space' -v expected='2' '{ name=$1; gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",name); if (name==key) { value=$2; sub(/[[:space:]]*[#;].*$/,\"\",value); gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",value) } } END { exit value != expected }' /etc/sysctl.conf 2>/dev/null ) && echo PASS || echo FAIL"
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*PASS\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "018, ASLR completo, Alta"
  info        : "Dificulta exploração de vulnerabilidades que dependem de previsibilidade de endereços."
  solution    : "Persistir o parâmetro em /etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf e aplicar com sysctl --system após validar a rede e a carga de trabalho."
  reference   : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  see_also    : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  cmd         : "( [ \"$(sysctl -n kernel.randomize_va_space 2>/dev/null)\" = \"2\" ] && grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*kernel\\.randomize_va_space[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*2([[:space:]]|$)' /etc/sysctl.d/99-hitss-hardening.conf 2>/dev/null && awk -F= -v key='kernel.randomize_va_space' -v expected='2' '{ name=$1; gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",name); if (name==key) { value=$2; sub(/[[:space:]]*[#;].*$/,\"\",value); gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",value) } } END { exit value != expected }' /etc/sysctl.conf 2>/dev/null ) && echo PASS || echo FAIL"
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*PASS\\s*$"
</custom_item>

<custom_item>
  type        : CMD_EXEC
  description : "019, perf_event restrito, Baixa"
  info        : "Perf counters podem ser usados para side channel e coleta de informacao de kernel."
  solution    : "Persistir o parâmetro em /etc/sysctl.d/99-hardening.conf e aplicar com sysctl --system após validar a rede e a carga de trabalho."
  reference   : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  see_also    : "01_Baseline_DEBLIKE_FULL_v1.0.0"
  cmd         : "( v=$(sysctl -n kernel.perf_event_paranoid 2>/dev/null); [ -n \"$v\" ] && [ \"$v\" -ge \"2\" ] && grep -Eq '^[[:space:]]*kernel\\.perf_event_paranoid[[:space:]]*=[[:space:]]*[2-9][0-9]*([[:space:]]|$)' /etc/sysctl.d/99-hitss-hardening.conf 2>/dev/null && awk -F= -v key='kernel.perf_event_paranoid' -v expected='2' '{ name=$1; gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",name); if (name==key) { value=$2; sub(/[[:space:]]*[#;].*$/,\"\",value); gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/,\"\",value) } } END { exit (value + 0) < (expected + 0) }' /etc/sysctl.conf 2>/dev/null ) && echo PASS || echo FAIL"
  expect      : "(?i)^\\s*PASS\\s*$"
</custom_item>

